tage only. This corrects the rejected source's unsupported nonlocal construct using a mutable local counter; no physical actions were acknowledged by that compilation failure. Measure the visible package top/table, validate a top-down contact model, and initialize a persistent cream-cheese patch tracker. Obtain visible approach clearance, measure actual opposed inner-pad gap before descent, close only once after an observed opposing contact position, and test retention with a 50 mm vertical lift. Success requires measured rigid following, a fresh observation of no slipping or other support, and a valid bottom-edge/table gap. Stop on uncertainty, occlusion, failed margins, stalled contact or command mismatch without automatic reopening. Slice limits are 22 controls and 66 native steps. No bowl alignment or deposit code is included.","source":"def main(api):
    key, m, count = "grasp_stage_v1", {}, [0]
    questions = {}
    for axis in ["x", "y", "z", "rx", "ry", "rz"]:
        questions[axis] = {"type": "choice", "instructions": "For this world position or world rotation-vector component use its explicit goal_relation: decrease means negative, increase means positive, within_tolerance means hold. Do not infer contact or unseen geometry.", "criteria": {"negative": "Decrease this world component.", "hold": "The component is within its supplied tolerance.", "positive": "Increase this world component."}}
    questions["gripper"] = {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Use objective.gripper exactly: open for open, close for close, keep for keep. Keep does not reopen a possibly held package. Closure is not retention evidence.", "criteria": {"open": "Deliver requested opening.", "close": "Deliver requested closing.", "keep": "Preserve the existing gripper command."}}

